# XSH posix_getdents
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
# posix_getdents() on a directory made by the test (files a, b, c, a long-
# named file, a subdirectory, a symbolic link, a FIFO). Names are compared
# with a readdir() listing of the same directory. d_type may be DT_UNKNOWN;
# when it is not, it must be the right kind. flags is 0.

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.001
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       Reading a directory to its end with a large buffer yields the same set of
           names as readdir() with every name once; for each entry d_ino equals
           st_ino of the file (of the link itself for a symbolic link), d_reclen is a
           multiple of the structure alignment, large enough for the name, and the
           entries tile the returned bytes exactly; d_type is DT_UNKNOWN or the right
           type.
test       t/001-entries.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.002
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       After the last entries are read, posix_getdents() returns 0, and returns 0
           again; after lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_SET) it returns the entries again.
test       t/002-end.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.003
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With nbyte only one byte more than sizeof(struct posix_dent) + {NAME_MAX},
           each call returns at least one entry, and repeated calls to the end return
           the same set of names as readdir(), none twice.
test       t/003-small-buffer.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.004
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
class      required
since      2024
says       posix_getdents() with nbyte 1 on a directory that has entries fails with
           EINVAL.
test       t/004-einval.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.005
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2024
says       posix_getdents() on descriptor -1 and on a closed descriptor fails with
           EBADF.
test       t/005-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.006
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#ERRORS/ENOTDIR
class      required
since      2024
says       posix_getdents() on a descriptor of a regular file opened for reading
           fails with ENOTDIR.
test       t/006-enotdir.c

assertion  XSH.posix_getdents.007
anchor     functions/posix_getdents.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       d_name of a file with a name of {NAME_MAX} bytes is that exact name;
           d_type of the symbolic link is DT_LNK or DT_UNKNOWN, never DT_REG or
           DT_DIR, and of the FIFO is DT_FIFO or DT_UNKNOWN.
test       t/007-names-types.c
